= Release History

== 2026-11-27 (SCALE-LETKF local changes)
* Bug fixes:
  * Port the fused vertical momentum fluxes and their total-velocity upwind selection from e016ebc73 [results change] (#3754).

== 2026-11-16 (SCALE-LETKF local changes)
* Improvements:
  * Port scale-met/scale#3634 (f621b9fdb, on top of #3633 42dc673da): new
    switches COMM_USE_NONPC_LAYOUT2 and COMM_USE_NONPC_BATCH in
    PARAM_COMM_CARTESC for the non-persistent halo exchange, .true. by
    default in OpenACC builds and .false. otherwise. COMM_USE_NONPC_LAYOUT2
    uses the layout 2 for the non-persistent 8-direction exchange of a 3-D
    variable (at most 16 requests instead of 12*JHALO+4; not with
    COMM_USE_MPI_ONESIDED). COMM_vars8_init without the array reserves an
    ID that is not bound to an array; such IDs can be declared as a group
    (COMM_vars_group_init), so that dummy arguments and arrays whose address
    is not fixed are exchanged in a batch (COMM_USE_NONPC_BATCH, which
    requires COMM_USE_BATCH: both must be switched off together in an
    OpenACC build). ATMOS_vars_fillhalo (5+QA), the fillhalo of the boundary
    variables and of their damping coefficients (5+BND_QA) and the
    tendencies exchanged in ATMOS_DYN_driver (4+QA) declare such groups.
    ATMOS_vars_fillhalo now posts all the variables before the waits, so
    COMM_vsize_max must be 5+QA or larger (the default is). In a batch the
    groups keep send and receive buffers for all the halos of their members.
    scale_comm_cartesC.F90 is the upstream file of f621b9fdb except for
    count_bytes, which does nothing here (no data size statistics of PROF).
    With it pack8_3D copies a variable that is not on the device for its
    kernel and waits for it there (#3633). The unit tests of upstream are
    imported except those of run-comm-dyn (unit_atmos_dyn_average is not in
    this tree). Upstream timings are not measurements of this port.
  * PROF items of the halo exchange, local change (not in upstream): an
    exchange with an ID that is not bound to an array is counted in COMM_vars
    and COMM_wait also when its group is exchanged in a batch. Upstream
    counts it in COMM_vars_pers and COMM_wait_pers there, so that the number
    of calls and the time move between the items with COMM_USE_NONPC_BATCH.

== 2026-11-15 (SCALE-LETKF local changes)
* Improvements:
  * Port scale-met/scale#3622 (c16a0141b) and #3623 (51afc9959): new
    switches COMM_USE_PC_LAYOUT2 and COMM_USE_BATCH in PARAM_COMM_CARTESC
    for the persistent halo exchange, .true. by default in OpenACC builds
    and .false. otherwise. The layout 2 sends the N/S halos as whole rows
    without packing and the corners only to the diagonal neighbors (at most
    16 requests for an 8-direction exchange instead of 28). The dynamics
    declares static groups of persistent variables (COMM_vars_group_init),
    whose messages are packed together with COMM_USE_BATCH (not in 2-D).
    A COMM_wait while a group is being posted stops with an error.
    scale_comm_cartesC.F90 is replaced by the upstream file, so that this
    tree also gets the upstream changes it builds on: communicators per
    grid and checks of the variable IDs (#3385), fixes of the one-sided
    communication (#3390), checks of the packing buffers in all builds and
    automatic extension of the persistent tables (#3426), COMM_vars_finalize
    (#3471, called by the driver and ATMOS_DYN_finalize), contiguity checks
    in debug builds, and SCALE_COMPAT_MPI (NO_MPI08) support in this file.
    The data size statistics of PROF are absent here, so they are not
    counted. The groups of the split-explicit variables of upstream are not
    declared, because this tree does not have them. LANDUSE_fillhalo uses
    the same two IDs for every PFT. The unit tests unit_comm_order and
    unit_comm_check and the upstream test_comm are imported; the dynamics
    tests of upstream (unit_atmos_dyn_average, unit_atmos_dyn_split) are not.
    Upstream timings are not measurements of this port.
  * Persistent halo exchange in batch, local changes after the port above
    (not in upstream). The packing kernel of a member of a group is not
    waited at its post: the kernels of all the members are waited once,
    when the last member is posted. A COMM_wait between the posts of a
    group now stops with an error only if it waits a member of that group;
    an exchange outside the group may be posted and waited there, provided
    that it is at the same place in all the processes (it hangs otherwise,
    and this is no longer detected). With this, the 15 fluxes of the
    numerical filter are one group (DYN_numfilter) instead of five, and the
    tendencies (two groups) and the tracers (one group) of the large step
    are declared. Warm bubble, 80x80x40 on 2x2 processes and 4 GPUs, 200
    steps: 65 -> 36 rounds and 520 -> 288 persistent sends per step and
    process, Main_Loop 7.06 -> 6.61 s (mean of 3, one node); the history
    and restart files are identical. Not measured in a real case.
  * The halo exchanges of calc_numdiff in the numerical filter of the
    tracers use the IDs 1 to 3 (as upstream) instead of 16 to 18, which are
    the IDs of the 11th to 13th tracers (without PROG) still in exchange in
    the tracer loop of the large step: with 12 or more tracers, the tracer
    filter and ND_LAPLACIAN_NUM >= 3, the check of the packing buffers
    (in all builds since the port above) stopped the run.

== 2026-11-14 (SCALE-LETKF local changes)
* Improvements:
  * Port scale-met/scale#3612 (0de3bc4a8, a4d4e88d1): reduce OpenACC
    sedimentation tracer-loop and terminal-velocity history overhead, and
    compute precipitation momentum transport over all grid points.
    Retain this tree's formulae and CPU loops; the upstream SPRINTARS work
    arrays are absent here. GPU FMA contraction may change rounding.
    Upstream timings are not measurements of this port.
  * Port scale-met/scale#3595 (571bc2ccd, f711a986c): compute upwind
    sedimentation and TOMITA08 terminal velocity over all grid points with
    OpenACC, and check the hydrometeor/charge tracer layout at setup.
    The formulae and CPU paths are retained. Upstream timings are not
    measurements of this port.

== 2024-04-10 (5.5.1)
* Bug fixes:
  * Fixed the mkinit for the baroclinic wave test case
  * Fixed a compile error for some version of GNU compiler
* Changes
  * Change default setting for MPI for FUJITSU compiler
* Updates:
  * Updated the user guide

== 2024-03-21 (5.5.0)
* Changes
  * Unified NetCDF file input module for the real input
  * Default use of domain center as the standard latitude for Mercator and equidistant cylindrical projections
  * Eliminated need to give the latlon catalog file
  * Eliminated need to give time information for boundary data
  * Eliminated need to give parent domain process information for offline nesting
  * Updated the namelist file and conversion script for the latest FNL data
  * Changed format of timer information in LOG file
  * Support newer version of GNU compiler
  * Addition and removal of several sysdef files
* New features
  * Added several options to the Tomita08 scheme
  * Added several options to the SN14 scheme
  * Added several options to the MYNN scheme
  * 2D parameters are available in the Kusaka01 scheme
  * User-defined calendar can be used
  * Added ability to output time min/max data to history file
  * Allowed relative paths to be set for bulk job
  * Tutorial simulations now support GPU computers
  * Supported one-sided MPI communication
* Improvements:
  * Improved iterations in the land and urban models
  * Improved numerical stability for the MYNN level 3 scheme
  * Improved handling of thermodynamical quantities in the KF scheme
  * Improved momentum flux calculation in the Kusaka01 scheme
  * Reduce memory usage in the real input
  * Optimization for the Fugaku supercomputer
  * Optimization of the SUZUKI10 scheme
* Bug fixes:
  * Fixed some bugs in SNO
  * Fixed many other bugs

